---
description: Database, Redis and object storage rules
globs:
  - "server/**/db/**"
  - "server/**/repository/**"
  - "server/src/main/resources/db/migration/**"
  - "infrastructure/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

- MySQL is the source of truth for persistent business data.
- Redis keys require a documented prefix, TTL and invalidation rule.
- Do not store permanent learner state only in Redis.
- Database changes require a new forward-only Flyway migration.
- Never edit an already released migration.
- Add indexes based on documented access patterns, not speculation.
- Use unique constraints for business idempotency where possible.
- Store audio metadata in MySQL and binary objects in S3-compatible storage.
- Avoid N+1 queries and unbounded list endpoints.
- Integration tests should use Testcontainers when practical.
